{# ============================================================================
   DRAFT - PENDING-APPROVALS ENTRY 32, USER'S PEN - REV-152 STAGED DRAFT.
   The pose-picker decision template (pose-picker.md REV-134e spec + the
   REV-136 consumer-model rulings): the decision model picks the pose WITHIN
   the already-selected category that best fits the scene context. Called from
   SkyrimNet_AnimationsGS.psc OnMuseConsideration's fire branch via
   SkyrimNetApi.SendCustomDecisionToLLM("ded/pose_picker", ...) after
   Sanguine's consideration call resolved the CATEGORY; the callback
   OnPosePicked fires the chosen event key through the existing hardened
   executor. This is NOT chat content: a decision template renders as a typed
   decision request (decisions LLM variant), not an NPC utterance.
   Options are DYNAMIC per call: the script passes the selected category's
   pose list (event key + per-pose description, poses.js = catalog of record)
   as the poseOptions array; each criteria line is "KEY: description", and
   the answer is the chosen event key alone. Wording ships draft-flagged per
   the standing register precedent (entries 15/16/26).
   ============================================================================ #}

[ state npc ]
{{ npcName }}, a {{ npcSex }}.
[ end state ]

[ state moment ]
Location: {{ location }}. Arousal: {{ arousal }}.
Pose policy this scene: {{ posePolicy }}.
Current pose state: {{ poseState }}.
[ end state ]

[ question pose choice ]
`npc` describes the NPC about to strike a pose. `moment` is the scene around
them right now. Choose the single pose from the options below that this NPC
would most plausibly perform at this exact moment -- the option whose
description best fits their arousal, the place, and what is going on. Answer
with one option key only.
[ criteria ]
{% for opt in poseOptions %}
{{ opt }}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
